      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate both sides of \\( x^{2} + y^{2} = 25 \\) with respect to \\( t \\), using the chain rule on each term: \\( \\left(2 x\\right)\\frac{dx}{dt} + \\left(2 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (3, 4) \\) the coefficient of \\( \\frac{dx}{dt} \\) is \\( 6 \\) and the coefficient of \\( \\frac{dy}{dt} \\) is \\( 8 \\). Substitute \\( \\frac{dx}{dt} = -2 \\): \\( (6)(-2) + (8)\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": -12
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Solve for the requested rate: \\( \\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
